  "research_conclusions_qa": {
    "Q1_is_buy_strength_predictive": "For XAU/USD: YES. Gold BUY strength demonstrates positive expectancy (+0.14R) with 45.4% win rate, surviving walk-forward testing. For BTC/USD: WEAK/NEGATIVE (-0.11R expectancy, 35.7% win rate), showing long setups underperformed due to macro chop/downtrends in 2023-2024.",
    "Q2_is_sell_strength_predictive": "For BTC/USD: YES. BTC SELL strength demonstrates solid predictive edge (+0.20R expectancy, 48.0% win rate, 1.38 PF). For XAU/USD: MODERATE (+0.08R expectancy, 43.3% win rate, 1.14 PF).",
    "Q3_is_higher_strength_associated_with_higher_future_win_rate": "On XAU/USD: YES, monotonic probability calibration is observed (50-59% strength -> 42.8% WR; 60-69% strength -> 47.9% WR; 70-79% strength -> 63.6% WR, PF 2.62). On BTC/USD: NON-MONOTONIC in raw confluence, but stabilizes when separated by SELL vs BUY direction.",
    "Q4_does_relationship_hold_for_btc": "Partially. It holds strongly for BTC SELL signals (+0.20R, PF 1.38), but BTC BUY signals suffered lower win rates (35.7%). Directional separation is mandatory.",
    "Q5_does_relationship_hold_for_xau": "YES. Gold demonstrates consistent statistical edge across all 4 walk-forward folds (+0.11R to +0.21R), with high stability and monotonic strength calibration.",
    "Q6_does_it_survive_walk_forward_testing": "YES. All 4 chronological walk-forward folds on both BTC and XAU delivered positive out-of-sample test expectancies (BTC test expectancies: +0.01R to +0.19R; XAU test expectancies: +0.11R to +0.21R).",
    "Q7_is_65_pct_threshold_statistically_defensible": "YES, as a filter for statistical bias edge. Threshold >=65% filters out noisy neutral regimes and captures signals with higher expectancy. However, because sample size at >=70% is currently modest (N ~ 10-25), requiring Delta >= 15% edge between BUY and SELL before triggering bias is statistically sound.",
    "Q8_is_there_evidence_of_lookahead_bias": "NO. Zero lookahead violations were detected across all 2,438 audited signals. 100% of historical samples used at timestamp T were completed prior to T.",
    "Q9_which_direction_performs_better": "BTC/USD: SELL performs substantially better (+0.20R vs -0.11R, PF 1.38 vs 0.83). XAU/USD: BUY performs better (+0.14R vs +0.08R, PF 1.25 vs 1.14).",
    "Q10_is_strength_calibrated_enough_to_be_used_as_probability": "NO. Strength score is an empirical multi-factor evidence score (0-100%), NOT a raw uncalibrated probability. Brier score (0.265-0.271) and ECE (~14-16%) confirm it must always be presented as an evidence score alongside calibrated odds.",
    "Q11_what_additional_data_is_required_before_production_changes": "1. Accumulate more point-in-time live trade samples in the >=70% bucket (currently N=10-15 per asset) to narrow the 95% Wilson confidence interval to < \u00b15%. 2. Maintain strict point-in-time isolation and avoid premature threshold tuning until N >= 100 in upper tiers."
